WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.900
Treasure Island

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:18.620
<i>There was no treasure!
Inside the chest was only a skull.</i>

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:22.540
<i>Enraged, the pirates attacked me!</i>

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:30.720
The chest is empty and you aren't the only ones who are angry!

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:34.180
So you better not annoy me!

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:45.920
Treasure
Island

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:45.720
Takarajima

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:54.530
saa ikou

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:54.530
Come, let's go

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:57.620
yume ni mita shima heto

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:57.620
To the island that I've dreamed of

00:00:57.870 --> 00:01:01.460
nami wo koete kaze ni notte

00:00:57.870 --> 00:01:01.460
Across the waves, on the wind

00:01:01.710 --> 00:01:04.340
umi hedeyou

00:01:01.710 --> 00:01:04.340
We'll travel the oceans

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:07.260
ikute ni wa

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:07.260
Many of us

00:01:07.510 --> 00:01:10.260
minna mada shiranai

00:01:07.510 --> 00:01:10.260
Still don't know of

00:01:10.510 --> 00:01:14.010
fushigi na hiru to yoru toga

00:01:10.510 --> 00:01:14.010
The days and nights full of mystery

00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:16.510
matte iru darou

00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:16.510
That await us there

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:20.020
itsumo shinji you

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:20.020
We must always have trust

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:23.270
magokoro wo

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:23.270
And be sincere

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:29.530
yuuki wo mune ni susumou yo

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:29.530
And have courage in our hearts to move forward

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:32.660
tade hitotsu no

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:32.660
I only...

00:01:32.990 --> 00:01:36.080
akogare dake wa

00:01:32.990 --> 00:01:36.080
...have one desire

00:01:36.330 --> 00:01:38.370
doko no dare ni mo

00:01:36.330 --> 00:01:38.370
And no one...

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:45.080
kese wa shinai sa

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:45.080
...will ever take it away

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:51.630
tade hitotsu no

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:51.630
I only...

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:54.930
akogare dake wa

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:54.930
...have one desire

00:01:55.180 --> 00:01:57.260
doko no dare ni mo

00:01:55.180 --> 00:01:57.260
And no one...

00:01:57.560 --> 00:02:04.190
kese wa shinai sa

00:01:57.560 --> 00:02:04.190
...will ever take it away

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:15.240
episode

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:15.240
\h      When a Pirate Dies,
He Leaves Only a Skeleton

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:32.390
Captain Silver.
What are we going to do now?

00:02:32.390 --> 00:02:36.380
We've dug ourselves to exhaustion for nothing.
We can't go on anymore.

00:02:36.710 --> 00:02:39.340
We've done everything you said.

00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:42.190
You must take responsibility.

00:02:42.190 --> 00:02:45.180
Yeah, take responsibility, Captain Silver!

00:02:45.590 --> 00:02:48.310
Take responsibility?

00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:49.980
How?

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:52.980
You want me to hang myself right here in front of you?

00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:55.430
Good idea.

00:02:55.430 --> 00:02:59.410
After all, you did receive the Black Spot.

00:03:09.330 --> 00:03:13.130
Idiot.
Don't get excited.

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:17.100
For 10 years I've searched for Flint's treasure.

00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:20.090
I won't abandon it so easily.

00:03:21.050 --> 00:03:22.290
It exists.

00:03:22.790 --> 00:03:25.010
It's somewhere on this island.

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:29.020
It's a riddle.
Old Flint has left us a riddle.

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:30.180
Isn't that right, Jim?

00:03:35.190 --> 00:03:41.230
In any case, Mr. Trelawney and Dr. Livesey knew that there was no treasure here.

00:03:41.230 --> 00:03:43.730
That much is obvious.

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:48.470
That's why they let us have the map.

00:03:48.470 --> 00:03:50.230
This leads me to think, Jim,

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:55.420
that you too, know the real location of the treasure.

00:03:56.920 --> 00:04:00.380
I agree with my men on this point.

00:04:00.870 --> 00:04:03.880
However, what sets George and me apart...

00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:05.870
...is our brains.

00:04:05.870 --> 00:04:11.160
That's why I won't attempt to make you talk using violence.

00:04:12.630 --> 00:04:14.590
This is what I propose...

00:04:14.590 --> 00:04:18.320
Tell me, Jim, what do you say about joining us?

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:20.680
You will obviously have a share of the treasure.

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:23.550
If you become a pirate at your age,

00:04:23.550 --> 00:04:26.220
you could even surpass the great Flint.

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:29.540
Like hell I will!

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:29.980
Like hell I will!

00:04:29.980 --> 00:04:30.240
Like hell I will!

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:30.910
Like hell I will!

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:38.870
Alright.

00:04:40.270 --> 00:04:42.260
Alright, Jim.

00:04:43.430 --> 00:04:46.710
Then I'll solve Flint's puzzle myself.

00:04:46.710 --> 00:04:49.390
That being the case,

00:04:49.390 --> 00:04:52.680
I won't talk to you anymore...

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:56.200
...and you'll stay tied up until we've found the treasure.

00:04:57.440 --> 00:05:00.400
Someone, tie him tightly to that tree!

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:02.410
R-Right, I'll do it!

00:05:05.270 --> 00:05:08.050
Guys, dig around.

00:05:08.050 --> 00:05:09.990
We're bound to find a clue!

00:05:09.990 --> 00:05:11.330
AYE!

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:33.430
They still don't understand and are back to digging.

00:05:34.590 --> 00:05:38.710
They can keep digging forever, they won't find anything.

00:05:38.710 --> 00:05:40.650
But this is Silver we're dealing with.

00:05:40.650 --> 00:05:42.440
Now that he has the map,

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:45.270
he could discover the paragraphs.

00:05:45.270 --> 00:05:46.770
I don't think so.

00:05:47.490 --> 00:05:48.970
What has he done to Jim?

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:52.450
He could be hungry, don't you think?

00:05:54.410 --> 00:05:58.750
I don't care whether these pirates find the treasure or not.

00:05:58.750 --> 00:06:02.680
The most important thing is to find a way to save Jim, Mr. Trelawney.

00:06:06.110 --> 00:06:08.080
Wh-Wh-What does that mean?!

00:06:08.080 --> 00:06:12.010
You dare to claim that
I don't care about Jim?!

00:06:12.510 --> 00:06:14.470
I said no such thing!

00:06:14.980 --> 00:06:18.390
But we aren't doing anything by just staying hidden here,

00:06:18.390 --> 00:06:20.900
is the point I'm trying to make!

00:06:20.900 --> 00:06:23.110
What do you mean by
just staying hidden?!

00:06:23.110 --> 00:06:26.070
"What do you mean by
just staying hidden?!"

00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:27.950
"I said no such thing."

00:06:28.990 --> 00:06:32.960
"But we aren't doing anything by just staying hidden here."

00:06:33.390 --> 00:06:35.070
"Wh-What does that mean?!"

00:06:35.070 --> 00:06:37.690
"You dare to claim that I don't care about Jim?"

00:06:38.190 --> 00:06:41.670
Just kidding.
Pretty good, aren't I?

00:06:41.670 --> 00:06:42.710
Very convincing.

00:06:42.710 --> 00:06:43.970
What talent...

00:06:44.950 --> 00:06:47.980
I used to be an impersonator in Paris.

00:06:50.070 --> 00:06:52.640
Alright, the coffee is ready.

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:54.950
Nothing like good coffee to calm yourself.

00:06:54.950 --> 00:06:58.510
It's a war of attrition.
We must wait until the right moment.

00:06:58.510 --> 00:07:00.850
I see no other solution.

00:07:01.950 --> 00:07:04.340
Isn't that right, Dr. Livesey?

00:07:05.830 --> 00:07:06.780
My, my.

00:07:07.530 --> 00:07:08.740
"My, my."

00:07:35.260 --> 00:07:37.930
<i>Alright...
Have it your way, Jim.</i>

00:07:37.930 --> 00:07:42.110
<i>That being the case,
I won't talk to you anymore!</i>

00:07:44.330 --> 00:07:46.310
<i>I won't talk to you either!</i>

00:07:46.810 --> 00:07:50.390
<i>Whatever he says, he's nothing but a pirate.</i>

00:07:50.390 --> 00:07:53.640
<i>A vulgar pirate obsessed with treasure.</i>

00:07:53.640 --> 00:07:56.570
<i>I'm the one that doesn't want to talk to you.</i>

00:08:04.070 --> 00:08:04.900
What happened?

00:08:04.270 --> 00:08:05.800
Hey, you alright?

00:08:07.070 --> 00:08:08.200
C-Captain!

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:09.830
It's horrible...

00:08:09.830 --> 00:08:11.290
Tattooed is dead.

00:08:11.290 --> 00:08:12.130
I see...

00:08:12.130 --> 00:08:15.500
Bury him in the hole he dug.

00:08:15.500 --> 00:08:16.810
Y-Yes, sir!

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:22.480
How much longer do we have to dig for?

00:08:22.480 --> 00:08:25.420
We still haven't found anything.

00:08:25.420 --> 00:08:27.910
Now what, "Great Captain Silver"??

00:08:27.910 --> 00:08:30.940
We don't want to end up like Tattooed!

00:08:31.250 --> 00:08:34.230
Still complaining?

00:08:34.230 --> 00:08:36.040
Do what I told you!

00:08:37.060 --> 00:08:40.040
I'm going to bury you alive if you don't shut up.

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:41.970
Wh-What?!

00:08:50.030 --> 00:08:52.010
We stay here tonight.
Understood?

00:09:35.630 --> 00:09:37.730
What do you think, Flint?

00:09:37.730 --> 00:09:41.230
There's no doubt this here is Captain Flint's treasure map.

00:09:41.230 --> 00:09:43.350
Yet, there's no treasure.

00:09:44.750 --> 00:09:46.520
What rotten luck...

00:09:46.520 --> 00:09:49.270
We haven't found any clues.

00:09:49.270 --> 00:09:52.690
Old Flint has left us a great riddle.

00:09:57.610 --> 00:10:02.670
He had six men help him bury the treasure.

00:10:02.670 --> 00:10:05.160
Of course, he had them all killed once the work was done.

00:10:05.160 --> 00:10:06.580
That's what he was like.

00:10:06.580 --> 00:10:11.140
This skull definitely belonged to one of Flint's six men.

00:10:11.140 --> 00:10:14.920
If he could talk, I'm sure
he would give us a clue.

00:10:31.560 --> 00:10:33.100
<i>That's it! I've found it!</i>

00:10:34.550 --> 00:10:36.360
<i>Look!
His left eye-socket!</i>

00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:39.320
<i>I thought that it was a wound, but it isn't!</i>

00:10:39.870 --> 00:10:41.480
<i>It's a clue left by Flint!</i>

00:11:08.070 --> 00:11:10.390
An arrow on the bone of his left eye-socket.

00:11:12.070 --> 00:11:16.740
It means the left eye of the skull on Skeleton Island. I'm sure of it!

00:11:20.950 --> 00:11:24.830
Get up, mates!
We depart for Skeleton Island!

00:11:25.780 --> 00:11:27.420
<i>Skeleton Island?</i>

00:11:41.270 --> 00:11:43.000
They're on the move again.

00:11:43.000 --> 00:11:45.390
Fine, then we shall follow them.

00:11:55.670 --> 00:11:58.070
But where can they go?

00:11:58.070 --> 00:12:00.990
I don't have the slightest idea.

00:12:00.990 --> 00:12:04.000
It seems they're watching Jim more closely than before.

00:12:04.630 --> 00:12:07.450
We can only follow them from afar.

00:12:36.150 --> 00:12:37.020
Bastard!

00:12:40.230 --> 00:12:41.310
Little brat!

00:12:43.310 --> 00:12:45.570
Wait, I'll take care of him!

00:12:46.250 --> 00:12:48.750
You'll wear yourselves out for nothing!

00:12:48.750 --> 00:12:50.490
Besides, you may get separated!

00:12:50.490 --> 00:12:53.790
Keep heading towards Skeleton Island.

00:12:53.790 --> 00:12:56.750
I'll return once I've caught him!

00:12:56.750 --> 00:12:57.710
Aye!

00:12:57.710 --> 00:12:58.720
Good!

00:13:24.870 --> 00:13:26.990
You should be more careful, Jim.

00:13:29.390 --> 00:13:30.950
That's quicksand you're in.

00:13:41.810 --> 00:13:45.220
Quicksand?
That was a close call!

00:13:45.220 --> 00:13:48.960
In fact, I lied.
It's just a small pond.

00:13:51.760 --> 00:13:54.140
Shut up! Shut up! Shut up! Shut up!

00:13:54.870 --> 00:13:56.920
Weren't you supposed to no longer talk to me?!

00:13:56.920 --> 00:13:59.400
So don't you talk to me!

00:14:00.860 --> 00:14:03.930
Yes, that's right.
I forgot.

00:14:04.630 --> 00:14:07.820
But let me give you just
one good piece of advice.

00:14:08.390 --> 00:14:10.860
If you want to run away, go in that direction.

00:14:10.860 --> 00:14:13.790
It won't be long until you join your friends...

00:14:13.790 --> 00:14:16.020
...if you go that way.

00:14:17.350 --> 00:14:18.500
See you.

00:14:22.350 --> 00:14:23.380
Silver!

00:14:24.840 --> 00:14:28.310
As a hostage, you were my trump card.

00:14:28.310 --> 00:14:30.110
I'd rather keep you,

00:14:30.110 --> 00:14:34.350
but my men are anxious and might take it out on you.

00:14:34.350 --> 00:14:37.810
I had to rough you up a bit
and tie you up. Bear with it.

00:14:38.200 --> 00:14:40.770
If I hadn't, it would've been hard to keep my men in check.

00:14:49.190 --> 00:14:50.740
Thanks.

00:14:54.810 --> 00:14:58.400
Fifteen men...

00:14:58.400 --> 00:15:02.940
...on a dead man's chest!

00:15:03.710 --> 00:15:08.880
Yo-ho-ho!
...and a bottle of rum!

00:15:09.610 --> 00:15:12.460
Drink and the devil...

00:15:12.460 --> 00:15:17.520
...had done for the rest!

00:15:17.520 --> 00:15:22.850
Yo-ho-ho!
...and another bottle of rum!

00:15:24.210 --> 00:15:26.530
They're heading towards Skeleton Island.

00:15:27.210 --> 00:15:28.250
Is Jim among them?

00:15:28.750 --> 00:15:31.160
Give me a sec!
Don't start that again!

00:15:33.490 --> 00:15:36.370
Too late, I can't see anything. They're too far away.

00:15:43.790 --> 00:15:45.790
<i>The left eye-socket...</i>

00:16:24.490 --> 00:16:28.210
Go on, guys!
Let's turn this cave upside down!

00:16:28.210 --> 00:16:30.840
Flint has obviously left us a clue here somewhere.

00:16:31.610 --> 00:16:32.720
Aye!

00:16:47.460 --> 00:16:49.670
It's like a labyrinth...

00:16:49.670 --> 00:16:51.610
This'll take us hours.

00:16:51.610 --> 00:16:53.740
Yes, what rotten luck.

00:16:56.900 --> 00:16:58.410
Hey, you alright, George?

00:16:58.410 --> 00:17:00.740
Darn it...
I cut myself.

00:17:03.330 --> 00:17:04.960
Damn it!

00:17:04.960 --> 00:17:06.680
I can't take anymore!
I'm gonna kill him!

00:17:07.850 --> 00:17:08.630
Wh-Who?

00:17:08.630 --> 00:17:12.750
Who do you think?
Silver, of course.

00:17:12.750 --> 00:17:16.130
You can't tell left from right in this cave.

00:17:16.130 --> 00:17:20.100
If we approach him from behind, we have a chance.

00:17:20.990 --> 00:17:22.670
H-Hey now...
W-Wait a moment.

00:17:22.670 --> 00:17:26.160
We have lots of time to do that after we find the treasure!

00:17:27.200 --> 00:17:32.190
Stupid! Do you really think that
Silver's going to share it with us?

00:17:32.190 --> 00:17:34.910
Remember, it was us who gave him the Black Spot.

00:17:34.910 --> 00:17:36.660
To him, we are the traitors.

00:17:36.660 --> 00:17:39.930
We're only alive because he needs us.

00:17:39.930 --> 00:17:42.580
He's never going to forgive us for it.

00:17:43.040 --> 00:17:44.960
Once he finds the treasure,

00:17:44.960 --> 00:17:48.080
he'll kill us and it'll be too late.

00:17:48.450 --> 00:17:50.100
We must do it quickly.

00:17:50.100 --> 00:17:53.810
We'll think of the treasure once he's out of the way!

00:17:54.610 --> 00:17:55.550
Well?

00:17:56.610 --> 00:18:00.510
Alright, I'm in.
Let's do it, George.

00:18:39.720 --> 00:18:43.100
<i>"Tell the truth with a flame."</i>

00:18:43.920 --> 00:18:46.150
"With a flame...", huh?

00:18:46.950 --> 00:18:48.060
<i>Of course!</i>

00:18:53.380 --> 00:18:56.990
Invisible ink!
That's the key to the puzzle!

00:18:59.840 --> 00:19:01.280
I-Invisible ink, you say?

00:19:01.280 --> 00:19:03.120
Yes...

00:19:03.120 --> 00:19:05.370
What a trickster, that Flint.

00:19:06.280 --> 00:19:08.330
Look!
It appeared!

00:19:09.080 --> 00:19:12.200
"A bell on the full-moon night..."

00:19:12.200 --> 00:19:13.710
"The mansion of Flint."

00:19:14.160 --> 00:19:18.090
"45 degrees with a spyglass on the Devil's Throne."

00:19:18.560 --> 00:19:22.050
"Aim the light through
the left eye of the skull."

00:19:22.050 --> 00:19:26.010
Wh-What does it mean?
It's sounds very eerie.

00:19:32.320 --> 00:19:33.190
Jim!

00:19:33.600 --> 00:19:35.610
Idiot!
What are you doing here?!

00:19:36.200 --> 00:19:38.070
Why didn't you escape?!

00:19:38.400 --> 00:19:40.030
Silver! Behind you!

00:19:47.200 --> 00:19:48.910
Silver!

00:19:52.640 --> 00:19:54.040
Die, Silver!

00:19:59.400 --> 00:20:00.750
Silver...

00:20:05.280 --> 00:20:09.100
Silver, you would have died sooner or later anyways.

00:20:09.100 --> 00:20:11.020
Go to hell!

00:20:15.000 --> 00:20:16.440
Wretched mortals...

00:20:17.640 --> 00:20:21.370
You will all go to hell together.

00:20:25.080 --> 00:20:26.280
That voice...!

00:20:26.280 --> 00:20:29.750
I-It's Flint!
It's the voice of Flint!

00:20:32.210 --> 00:20:33.670
Come...

00:20:34.080 --> 00:20:36.610
Come and join me in hell!

00:20:42.300 --> 00:20:45.010
It's the ghost of Flint!

00:20:54.560 --> 00:20:57.090
Yes, it is I, Flint!

00:20:59.480 --> 00:21:03.490
Good, now's our chance!
Let's rescue Jim! Charge!

00:21:04.480 --> 00:21:06.660
Forward!

00:21:08.200 --> 00:21:09.530
There you are!

00:21:24.260 --> 00:21:25.760
Curses!

00:21:25.760 --> 00:21:27.800
Break through!

00:21:48.480 --> 00:21:52.520
Jim, why did you follow me?

00:21:52.520 --> 00:21:53.830
B-Because...

00:21:54.360 --> 00:21:55.750
I don't know either!

00:21:56.990 --> 00:22:00.510
Besides, I-I didn't follow you!

00:22:00.510 --> 00:22:03.980
That's not it at all!
Y-You're wrong!

00:22:05.330 --> 00:22:06.530
Am I?

00:22:07.610 --> 00:22:08.760
Stop laughing!

00:22:08.760 --> 00:22:10.270
Leave him be, Jim.

00:22:10.270 --> 00:22:12.070
Let him laugh if he wants to.

00:22:12.070 --> 00:22:14.900
Arrogant as he may be,
he's now our prisoner.

00:22:17.310 --> 00:22:18.950
Silver, don't forget.

00:22:18.950 --> 00:22:22.950
Your life is now in our hands.

00:22:24.140 --> 00:22:28.490
I see. The situation has
taken an interesting turn.

00:22:28.310 --> 00:22:32.160
To      be        continued

00:22:33.270 --> 00:22:38.310
shiokaze yo omae mo

00:22:33.270 --> 00:22:38.310
Hey sea breeze

00:22:38.310 --> 00:22:44.120
tomodachi naraba tsutaete

00:22:38.310 --> 00:22:44.120
If you're my friend then carry

00:22:45.340 --> 00:22:50.330
furusato ni nokoshite kita

00:22:45.340 --> 00:22:50.330
To my home that I've left behind

00:22:50.330 --> 00:22:55.770
natsukashii haha ni hitokoto

00:22:50.330 --> 00:22:55.770
A word to my dear mother

00:22:55.770 --> 00:23:01.180
boku wa genki de yattemasu

00:22:55.770 --> 00:23:01.180
Tell her that I'm doing fine

00:23:01.180 --> 00:23:06.640
kaban ippai no

00:23:01.180 --> 00:23:06.640
And that my bag filled

00:23:06.640 --> 00:23:12.270
nozomi to yume to takaramono

00:23:06.640 --> 00:23:12.270
With hopes, dreams and treasures

00:23:12.270 --> 00:23:18.130
kakaete kaeritai

00:23:12.270 --> 00:23:18.130
Will be brought back

00:23:19.220 --> 00:23:24.720
yuuyake wo senaka ni

00:23:19.220 --> 00:23:24.720
The sunset on my back

00:23:24.720 --> 00:23:30.610
kamome wo kata ni tomarasete

00:23:24.720 --> 00:23:30.610
And a seagull perched on my shoulder

00:23:30.610 --> 00:23:40.330
boku wa fukimasu kuchibue wo

00:23:30.610 --> 00:23:40.330
I blow out a whistle

00:23:45.140 --> 00:23:48.630
The invincible Silver has caught malaria.

00:23:48.630 --> 00:23:51.940
The only cure is a strange water lily.

00:23:51.940 --> 00:23:53.660
But who's going to go search for it?

00:23:54.300 --> 00:23:58.120
"Seagull" Puppy volunteers himself.
Can you believe it?

00:23:58.820 --> 00:24:00.940
Will he find the water lily flower?

00:24:00.940 --> 00:24:04.710
Next time on Treasure Island:
"The Flying Man—Puppy the Seagull!"

00:24:04.710 --> 00:24:07.810
Fly! Fly! Fly!
Swirl... Swirl!

